{"name":"Dynamo","hex":"#953d68","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Dynamo","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["Dynamo Sports Club, a national sporting association in the Soviet Union, and other similiar organisations in other socialist countries and their successor states.","Any of various football clubs and other sports teams linked to a Dynamo association, including Dynamo Berlin, Dynamo Dresden, Dynamo Kyiv and Dinamo Zagreb in soccer and HC Dynamo Moscow in ice hockey."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Dynamo"}],"entries":[{"title":"Dynamo","blocks":[{"text":"A dynamo is an electrical generator that creates direct current using a commutator, and uses self-powering electromagnets for the stator field rather than permanent magnets. Dynamos are self-starting by using residual magnetic field left in the iron cores of the electromagnets. If a dynamo were never run before, it was usual to use a separate battery to excite or flash the field of the electromagnets to enable self-starting. Dynamos were the first practical electrical generators capable of delivering power for industry, and the foundation upon which many other later electric-power conversion devices were based, including the electric motor, the alternating-current alternator, and the rotary converter."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/14/DynamoElectricMachinesEndViewPartlySection_USP284110.png/330px-DynamoElectricMachinesEndViewPartlySection_USP284110.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dynamo"},{"title":"Dynamo (Soda Stereo album)","blocks":[{"text":"Dynamo is the sixth studio album by Argentinian rock band Soda Stereo. It was first released in Argentina on 26 October 1992 by Sony Music Argentina."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/8/85/Soda_Stereo_-_Dynamo_%28Album_cover%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dynamo_(Soda_Stereo_album)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/19/Faraday_disk_generator.jpg/500px-Faraday_disk_generator.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/19/Faraday_disk_generator.jpg/1280px-Faraday_disk_generator.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/19/Faraday_disk_generator.jpg/500px-Faraday_disk_generator.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The Faraday disk was the first electric generator. The horseshoe-shaped magnet (A) created a magnetic field through the disk (D). When the disk was turned, this induced an electric current radially outward from the center toward the rim.  The current flowed out through the sliding spring contact m (connected to B') through the external circuit, and back through B to the center of the disk through the axle","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AFaraday_disk_generator.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/10/Wechselstromerzeuger_Crop_LevelAdj.jpg/500px-Wechselstromerzeuger_Crop_LevelAdj.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/10/Wechselstromerzeuger_Crop_LevelAdj.jpg/500px-Wechselstromerzeuger_Crop_LevelAdj.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Hippolyte Pixii's dynamo. The commutator is located on the shaft below the spinning magnet","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AWechselstromerzeuger_Crop_LevelAdj.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a8/Pacinotti_dynamo.jpg/500px-Pacinotti_dynamo.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a8/Pacinotti_dynamo.jpg/1280px-Pacinotti_dynamo.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a8/Pacinotti_dynamo.jpg/500px-Pacinotti_dynamo.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Pacinotti dynamo, 1860","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APacinotti_dynamo.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/52/Thinktank_Birmingham_-_object_1889S00044%281%29.jpg/500px-Thinktank_Birmingham_-_object_1889S00044%281%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/52/Thinktank_Birmingham_-_object_1889S00044%281%29.jpg/500px-Thinktank_Birmingham_-_object_1889S00044%281%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":" The Woolrich Electrical Generator in Thinktank, Birmingham ","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AThinktank_Birmingham_-_object_1889S00044(1).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6b/Gramme_dynamo.png/500px-Gramme_dynamo.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6b/Gramme_dynamo.png/500px-Gramme_dynamo.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Small Gramme dynamo, around 1878","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AGramme_dynamo.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/70/High-Current_Copper-Brush_Commutated_Dynamo.jpg/500px-High-Current_Copper-Brush_Commutated_Dynamo.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/70/High-Current_Copper-Brush_Commutated_Dynamo.jpg/1280px-High-Current_Copper-Brush_Commutated_Dynamo.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/70/High-Current_Copper-Brush_Commutated_Dynamo.jpg/500px-High-Current_Copper-Brush_Commutated_Dynamo.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Low voltage dynamo for electroplating from the turn of the century.  The resistance of the commutator contacts causes inefficiency in low voltage, high current machines like this, requiring a huge elaborate commutator.  This machine generated 7 volts at 310 amps.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AHigh-Current_Copper-Brush_Commutated_Dynamo.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/b/bd/Cerati_performing_in_1993.jpg/250px-Cerati_performing_in_1993.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/b/bd/Cerati_performing_in_1993.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/b/bd/Cerati_performing_in_1993.jpg/250px-Cerati_performing_in_1993.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Guitarist and singer Gustavo Cerati (pictured) performing with Soda Stereo in Mexico City, 1993","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACerati_performing_in_1993.jpg"}],"sounds":{},"pictures":[]}}